
```

---

### **2. The `.gitignore` Files**

Since you have multiple languages (Node/Python) and environments, it is best to have **one `.gitignore` per folder**, or a master one at the root.

Here is the **Master Root `.gitignore`** (Place this in the root folder):

```gitignore
# --- Node.js (Client & Server) ---
node_modules/
dist/
build/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Python (Analytics Service) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
env/
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Environment Variables (CRITICAL) ---
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

# --- OS Files ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Testing ---
coverage/


.Analytics_service/.env
**/.env


